                <pb facs="0133" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3582: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Nicholson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-04T22:00:00-04:00">March 4, 1934—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 4—2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. My telegram No. 13, February 27, 11 p.m. Official Paraguayan reply to League
                    Commission virtually refuses peace proposal, chief objection as stated in my
                    telegram referred to. Full text by air mail.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires and La Paz.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nicholson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
